(1) Express the area of the shaded part using an algebraic expression; 
(2) When \(a=10\) and \(b=4\), find the area of the shaded part.

In the figure, AB is the diameter of circle O, and it intersects chord CD at point E. We present the following conclusions: 
1. AE • BE = CE • DE; 
2. Triangle ADE is similar to triangle CBE; 
3. Angle A = Angle C; 
4. Angle AED = Angle BEC. 
Which of these conclusions are correct? ( )

In the cube \(ABCD-A_{1}B_{1}C_{1}D_{1}\), points \(E\), \(F\), and \(G\) are the midpoints of segments \(A_{1}B_{1}\), \(B_{1}C_{1}\), and \(BB_{1}\) respectively. Given the following four statements: 
1. \(FG\) is parallel to plane \(AA_{1}D_{1}D\); 
2. \(EF\) is parallel to plane \(BC_{1}D_{1}\); 
3. \(FG\) is parallel to plane \(BC_{1}D_{1}\); 
4. Plane \(EFG\) is parallel to plane \(BC_{1}D_{1}\). 
Which of the statements are correct? (Choose the correct numbers)
A. 1 and 3
B. 1 and 4
C. 2 and 3
D. 2 and 4

